sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Edge as Edge Service (gate/camera)
    participant API as POST /api/v1/parking-events
    participant Filter as GateApiKeyAuthFilter (X-Gate-Key)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Outbox as Outbox Relay
    participant MQ as RabbitMQ

    Edge->>Filter: HTTPS multipart/JSON<br/>X-Gate-Key: <per-camera key>
    Filter->>Filter: resolve camera_id from key, reject if unknown/disabled
    Filter->>API: authenticated request (no JWT)
    API->>API: validate payload (event_type, eventId, occurredAt, tenant/site scope)
    API->>DB: SELECT 1 FROM parking_event WHERE event_id = ?
    alt already processed
        DB-->>API: row exists
        API-->>Edge: 200 OK (idempotent replay)
    else new event
        API->>DB: BEGIN TX
        API->>DB: INSERT parking_event
        API->>DB: INSERT outbox_message (same TX)
        opt multipart snapshot present
            API->>API: store snapshot (object storage / local disk in dev)
            API->>DB: INSERT snapshot row (same TX)
        end
        API->>DB: COMMIT
        API-->>Edge: 202 Accepted {event_id}
        Outbox->>DB: poll PENDING outbox_message
        Outbox->>MQ: publish(routingKey, payload)
        MQ-->>Outbox: ack
        Outbox->>DB: mark DISPATCHED
    end

    Note over Edge,Filter: On network failure, Edge retries from its SQLite<br/>store-and-forward queue using the same eventId.
